# An atom that names nothing stays a word: a path through it reads no field -- answer 3 (plan M11 5a).
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and reads
# the Structures by paths through main\data. main has no code, so there is no call: its part code is the empty `()`.
sub: main () (
    Struct1: Nothing
) ()
int: seen main\data\Struct1\Nothing\v
